<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A now-playing card: cover art, the title and artist with a favorite toggle, a seek bar with elapsed and remaining
time, and shuffle / previous / play-pause / next / repeat controls. A **block** composed from
[Toggle](<%= page_path(:toggle) %>), [Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>), [Slider](<%= page_path(:slider) %>) and
Icon, as on the [Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui).

<%= embed Blocks::MusicPlayerPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
MusicPlayer(title: track.title, artist: track.artist, album: track.album, cover: track.cover_url,
  duration: track.duration, src: track.audio_url)
```

- With `src:` the block plays the audio: play / pause drive it, the seek bar jumps in it and follows its time.
- Without `src:` the demo advances the time once a second while playing.
- At the end of the track it starts over while **Repeat** is pressed, otherwise it stops.
- Previous and next restart the track and emit `blocks--music-player:previous` / `:next` - load the other track
  there (e.g. with a Turbo Frame).

```js
document.addEventListener("blocks--music-player:next", () => Turbo.visit("/player/next", { frame: "player" }))
```

## Events

| Event | Detail | When |
|-------|--------|------|
| `blocks--music-player:play` / `:pause` | - | The play button is toggled. |
| `blocks--music-player:seek` | `{ position }` | The seek bar moves (seconds). |
| `blocks--music-player:previous` / `:next` | - | The skip buttons are pressed. |
| `ui--toggle:change` | `{ pressed }` | Favorite, shuffle or repeat is toggled. |

## Localization

`music_player.locales.yml` holds the button and slider labels (English, Czech, German, Arabic); the play button's
label switches between "Play" and "Pause".

